# CatalogService API test suite - DEV / no JWT
# IntelliJ IDEA Ultimate HTTP Client
#
# HOW TO USE
# 1) Run CatalogService with profile "dev".
# 2) For the cleanest result, use a clean/dev database before "Run All Requests in File".
# 3) Run requests from top to bottom. Positive create requests capture IDs used later.
# 4) Lines marked EXPECT 4xx are intentional negative/business-validation tests.
#
# IMPORTANT
# - This suite contains both happy-path and negative tests.
# - A 400/404/409 marked EXPECT is a PASS for that test case.
# - Dynamic UUID variables can still trigger harmless IntelliJ OpenAPI inspections.
# - LocalDateTime values intentionally use Spring's ISO_LOCAL_DATE_TIME format.
# - No JWT header is required when SecurityConfigDev permits all requests.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8083/api/v1
@page = 0
@size = 20
@missingUuid = 11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
@missingUuid2 = 22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222
@missingInt = 2147483647


### ============================================================
### 0. INFRASTRUCTURE
### ============================================================

### 0.1 OpenAPI JSON - EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================
### 1. REGION
### ============================================================

### 1.1 Create Region - EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/regions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Region {{$timestamp}}",
  "slug": "http-region-{{$timestamp}}"
}

> {%
client.global.set("regionId", String(response.body["data"]["id"]));
client.global.set("regionName", String(response.body["data"]["name"]));
client.global.set("regionSlug", String(response.body["data"]["slug"]));
%}


### 1.2 Get Region by ID - EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/regions/{{regionId}}
Accept: application/json


### 1.3 Get all Regions - EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/regions?page={{page}}&size={{size}}
Accept: application/json


### 1.4 Update Region - EXPECT 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/regions/{{regionId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "HTTP Region Updated {{$timestamp}}"
}


### 1.5 Create duplicate Region using existing slug - EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/regions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Another HTTP Region {{$timestamp}}",
  "slug": "{{regionSlug}}"
}


### 1.6 Create Region with blank name - EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/regions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "slug": "invalid-blank-region-{{$timestamp}}"
}


### 1.7 Get nonexistent Region - EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/regions/{{missingInt}}
Accept: application/json


